        {
          "type": "text",
          "layout": "rail",
          "title": "UI Scene Transition",
          "body": "Rather than treating each screen change as an isolated transition, the home, out-of-game and in-game interfaces form one continuous spatial event. Sea level, sky and the island's overhead view are connected through upward and downward camera tilts, carrying the player continuously between the home, out-of-game, in-game and pause states. This camera language strengthens the worldbuilding and turns interface changes into one coherent seafaring adventure.",
          "highlights": [
            {
              "text": "one continuous spatial event",
              "tone": "dark"
            },
